<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/glossary#qatar-and-dubai-riyal">Glossary</a> · Term · currency</p><h1 class="enc-title">Qatar and Dubai riyal</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1966–1973</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as Qatar-Dubai riyal</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Qatar and Dubai riyal was the currency issued jointly by Qatar and Dubai from 1966 to 1973. It replaced the Gulf <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rupee">rupee</a> after <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a> devalued the rupee in 1966, and was itself replaced by the Qatari riyal in Qatar and by the UAE dirham in Dubai and the other <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/emirate">emirates</a> after the federation was formed.</p></div>
